*.pyc

# Secrets. .env.* covers the variants people actually create by hand — .env.bak,
# .env.old, .env.production, a dated copy made before reinstalling — any one of which
# holds a live API key and, unlike .env itself, was not ignored before. .env.example
# is the tracked template and is deliberately exempt.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# BMO runtime state — personal data, not source.
# scratch/ caches images and files you send BMO (including photos).
scratch/

# Photos, wherever they land. scratch/ above only covers BMO's own cache; this repo's
# history once carried 19 phone JPEGs with GPS coordinates in EXIF, staged from outside
# it by an agent running `git add -A`. The tracked images are all PNG app assets, so no
# legitimate file is lost here. githooks/pre-commit is the real guard — it checks magic
# bytes rather than trusting a file extension; this is just the cheap first layer.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.heif
history.json
memory.db
runtime_state.json

# Piper voice models are large and optional — see public/voices/README.md
public/voices/*.onnx
public/voices/*.onnx.json

# Local agent/tool scratch — not part of the project
.gemini/

# BMO writes what it learns about you here — seeded from MEMORY.example.md
MEMORY.md

# BMO's personality, yours to tune — seeded from SOUL.example.md on first run.
# Untracked on purpose: this file used to be tracked, so `git pull` fought every
# customisation you made. The tool-calling protocol that used to live alongside it now
# sits in AGENTS.md, which stays tracked and keeps updating.
SOUL.md
